From dd346a9612d70d8138d94399240294d688a7afc0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gibryon Bhojraj <gibryon@treeswift.com>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 21:27:15 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] panel: Request the output's width for the layer surface

The panel asked for a width of 0, leaving the width to the compositor.
Before the compositor knows the size it placed the surface with,
Mir (Ubuntu Frame) places it at its default 640x480 window size,
so the first configure sent to the panel has a width of 0
and the exclusive zone briefly reserves 480 pixels.
Applications squeezed into the remaining space resize twice
each time the panel opens: on an 800 pixel tall screen,
to 320 and then to the correct 534.

The panel always spans its output, so request that width.
If the output's size is not known, the width stays 0 as before.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/animation.rs |  2 ++
 src/panel.c      |  9 +++++----
 src/panel.rs     | 41 +++++++++++++++++++++++++----------------
 src/state.rs     | 18 +++++++++++++++---
 4 files changed, 47 insertions(+), 23 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/animation.rs b/src/animation.rs
index 61b6c3f..45fed84 100644
--- a/src/animation.rs
+++ b/src/animation.rs
@@ -29,6 +29,8 @@ pub enum Outcome {
     Visible {
         output: OutputId,
         height: PixelSize,
+        /// Width of the output. The panel spans all of it.
+        width: PixelSize,
         contents: Contents,
     },
     Hidden,
diff --git a/src/panel.c b/src/panel.c
index a9942c8..8b947fe 100644
--- a/src/panel.c
+++ b/src/panel.c
@@ -58,9 +58,9 @@ make_widget (struct panel_manager *self)
 // Called also from rust
